# Files that check-files.sh lets past its 1 MiB limit, one per line, in
# sha256sum's format: the sha256 of the file's bytes, two spaces, then its
# exact path from the repo root. A file passes only when both match one line;
# the same bytes at another path, or other bytes at this path, are refused like
# any other large file. The media rule still applies to every file.
#
# Adding, changing or removing a line is a check change: it goes in its own
# change, with a "Check changes:" line in the PR. Updating a file listed here
# means replacing its line with the new sha256, in the same way.

# wordfreq v3.2's English word list, unmodified, for the C4 term lookup (#148).
